<title>FRANCE: U.S. principal destination for Paris Nov exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. principal destination for Paris Nov exports.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, Jan 8 (Reuter) The United States was the principal country of destination for export traffic handled at the Paris airports in November 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading destinations by country for ADP exports in November 1996, with percentage change on November 1995, in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	 12,120 tonnes  up    9.6 pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan		    2,730 tonnes  down 17.5</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		2,690 tonnes  up   37.9</p>
<p> 4  Germany		  1,918 tonnes  up   26.7</p>
<p> 5  United Kingdom	 1,886 tonnes  up   39.7</p>
<p> 6  Canada		   1,783 tonnes  down 16.4</p>
<p> 7  Brazil		   1,594 tonnes  up   31.2</p>
<p> 8  UAE			1,446 tonnes  up   71.3</p>
<p> 9  Mexico		   1,276 tonnes  up   30.4</p>
<p> 10 Singapore		1,142 tonnes  up   91.2</p>
<p> 11 India			973 tonnes  down 22.9</p>
<p> 12 French West Indies     941 tonnes  down 10.9</p>
<p> 13 Egypt			912 tonnes  up   43.7</p>
<p> 14 Italy			871 tonnes  up   36.4</p>
<p> 15 Reunion		    769 tonnes  down 19.8</p>
<p> 16 Saudi Arabia	     756 tonnes  down 23.4</p>
<p> 17 Korea			736 tonnes  up    2.9</p>
<p> 18 South Africa	     732 tonnes  up   11.4</p>
<p> 19 Thailand		   681 tonnes  up    9.3</p>
<p> 20 Vietnam		    578 tonnes  up   94.0</p>
<p> Total			36,534 tonnes</p>
<p>Global November 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports, totalled 53,724 tonnes, up 8.4 percent on the same month the previous year, ADP said. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
